          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क़ैद — qaid — \"imprisonment, a prison sentence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अदालत ने चोर को दो साल की क़ैद सुनाई। adālat ne cor ko do sāl kī qaid sunāī. The court sentenced the thief to two years in prison."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क़ैद (qaid) is usually traced to Arabic qayd, \"a fetter, a bond\", which reached Hindi through Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
